<section class="shell band faq">
  <h2>Questions about equine therapy</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>Do I ride the horse?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>No. All of the work is on the ground. This is equine-assisted psychotherapy, not
      therapeutic riding, and no riding experience is needed or wanted.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Where do the equine sessions happen?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Near Dripping Springs, Texas, roughly forty minutes from central Austin. The specific
      location is arranged with you once the online sessions are done.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Who is the horse?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Blu, a bay gelding, near Dripping Springs. You work with him on the ground. He has no
      routine to run through and nothing to demonstrate; what he does is respond to your state,
      which is what makes the session useful.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Do I need experience with horses?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>None at all. Most people arrive with no horse experience, and the session is built
      around noticing rather than skill. Being nervous around horses is workable material, not a
      disqualification, but it should be something you choose to walk toward.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Can I start with an equine session?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>No. {% include "partials/text/in-person-prereq.njk" %} The pacing and the working relationship are
      established before the setting changes.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Is equine therapy available for teenagers?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>No. These sessions are for adults 18 and over. The practice does not work with young
      children and does not offer in-person sessions to anyone under 18.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
